    {
      "name": "Solicitações",
      "description": "Solicitações (tickets). JWT-protected edges that forward to the Exati IoT Hub Solicitações API (docs: https://iothub-solicitacoes.apidog.io — criar/consultar/cancelar). On the certifier the outbound base URL embeds the product token (`/tickets/<token>`) and the server sends the `client-address` header (gateway UUID); both are configured server-side via `exati.tickets.*`, not sent from Postman. Requires `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` (run **Auth → Register/Login** first).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Solicitação",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/solicitacoes",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "solicitacoes"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"device_uuid\": \"6f7f4c6d-0d6e-4f2b-8d58-3c0d3d92f1a1\",\n  \"id_external_protocol\": 987654,\n  \"external_protocol\": \"PROTOCOLO-987654\",\n  \"service_code\": \"ILUMINACAO_FALHA\",\n  \"nameplate_num\": \"PLACA-4458\",\n  \"description\": \"Luminária apagada durante a noite\",\n  \"justification\": \"Abertura automática para atendimento\",\n  \"address\": \"Rua das Acácias, 120\",\n  \"latitude\": \"-23.550520\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-46.633308\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Create a solicitação (ticket) on the Exati IoT Hub Solicitações API.\n\n**Required fields**\n- `device_uuid` (UUID)\n- `id_external_protocol` (number ≥ 1)\n- `external_protocol` (string)\n- `service_code` (string)\n\nOptional: `nameplate_num`, `description`, `justification`, `address`, `latitude`, `longitude`. Validation runs before any outbound call, so bad input fails fast as a local 400.\n\n**Status codes** (mirrors upstream)\n- `201 Created` — body has `id_external_protocol`, `id_ticket`, `device_uuid`, `ticket_status`\n- `200 OK` — idempotent repeat: a ticket with the same parameters already exists\n- `400 Bad Request` — local bean validation failure, or Exati `INVALID_HEADER`\n- `401 Unauthorized` — JWT missing/invalid/expired\n- `403 Forbidden` — Exati `CLIENT_OR_VENDOR_IDENTIFICATION_MISSING`\n- `404 Not Found` — Exati `ENTITY_NOT_FOUND`\n- `409 Conflict` — Exati `RESOURCE_CONFLICT` / `DEVICE_IS_NOT_AVAILABLE` / `INVALID_STATE`\n- `422 Unprocessable Entity` — Exati `INVALID_PARAMETERS`\n- `429 Too Many Requests` — Exati `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (concurrent request for the same protocol)\n- `502 Bad Gateway` — Exati unreachable, 5xx, or `VENDOR_REQUEST_ERROR`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 201 or 200 (idempotent)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('id_ticket returned', () => pm.expect(body.id_ticket).to.be.a('number'));",
                  "pm.test('ticket_status present', () => pm.expect(body.ticket_status).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "201 Created",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"device_uuid\": \"6f7f4c6d-0d6e-4f2b-8d58-3c0d3d92f1a1\",\n  \"id_external_protocol\": 987654,\n  \"external_protocol\": \"PROTOCOLO-987654\",\n  \"service_code\": \"ILUMINACAO_FALHA\"\n}"
